{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Great! I can see that the baseline (P0) scores 0.03167, and the current version improves slightly to 0.03079. Now I'll implement some improvements based on the dataset characteristics.\n\nLooking at the data, I notice:\n1. There are categorical columns that should be encoded properly\n2. Some numerical columns might benefit from transformations\n3. The target classes are imbalanced (class 0 has 456 samples vs class 4 only 5)\n4. Some columns seem to have similar meanings or could be combined\n\nLet me create an improved pipeline:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6d94fda9e3ec4760b9bedb6e","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"pipeline.py","edits":"[{\"oldText\": \"\"\"\"\"\"\", \"newText\": \"\"\"import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction import DictVectorizer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n\nMODEL_KWARGS = {}  # constructor settings for the frozen model; {} keeps the defaults\n\n\ndef preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Handle categorical variables by encoding them\n    # First, identify categorical columns\n    categorical_columns = X_train.select_dtypes(include=['category', 'object']).columns.tolist()\n    \n    # Fit label encoders on training data and transform both train and test\n    le_dict = {}\n    for col in categorical_columns:\n        if col in X_train.columns:\n            le = LabelEncoder()\n            # Fit on train + test to handle unseen categories\n            combined_data = pd.concat([X_train[col], X_test[col]], ignore_index=True)\n            le.fit(combined_data)\n            le_dict[col] = le\n            \n            # Transform train and test\n            X_train[col] = le.transform(X_train[col])\n            X_test[col] = le.transform(X_test[col])\n    \n    return X_train, y_train, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Create